  "evidencia": "Page: Iphigénie en Tauride. Sentence: Iphigénie en Tauride (\"Iphigenia in Tauris\") is a 1779 opera by Christoph Willibald Gluck in four acts.\nPage: Der Barbier von Bagdad. Sentence: Der Barbier von Bagdad (\"The Barber of Baghdad\") is a comic opera in two acts by Peter Cornelius to a German libretto by the composer, based on \"The Tale of the Tailor\" and \"The Barber’s Stories of his Six Brothers\" in \"One Thousand and One Nights\".\nPage: Nicolas-François Guillard. Sentence: His most famous work is \"Iphigénie en Tauride\", his first libretto, set by Gluck after the composer had initially rejected it.\nPage: Chimène. Sentence: It takes the form of a \"tragédie (lyrique)\" in three acts, with a libretto by Nicolas-François Guillard.",
